<title>USA: CME February volume falls 13.7 pct year-on-year.</title>
<headline>CME February volume falls 13.7 pct year-on-year.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange (CME) said volume in February totaled 15,754,916 contracts, down 13.7 percent from the year-ago monthly level of 18,248,672 contracts.</p>
<p>Open interest at month's end stood at 6,821,000, up 6.4 percent from 6,408,847 at the end of February last year.</p>
<p>Major categories were as follows:</p>
<p>Futures (individual)   Feb 1997	% change	   Feb 1996</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   7,535,653	  -26.5	  10,255,864</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   573,742	   +4.0	     551,824</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   458,027	  +11.1	     412,270</p>
<p>  Swiss franc	    317,642	   +7.4	     295,659</p>
<p>  British pound	  168,919	  -37.5	     270,247</p>
<p>  Canadian dollar	127,397	   +2.2	     124,654</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		1,429,921	  -26.1	   1,935,984</p>
<p>  Live cattle	    356,042	  +27.4	     279,526</p>
<p>  Live/lean hogs	 163,295	  +16.7	     139,887</p>
<p>Options on futures</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   1,932,586	   +4.5	   1,849,158</p>
<p>  Eurodollar midcurve  775,798	 +258.1	     216,622</p>
<p>  British pound	   62,491	  -69.5	     204,820</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   196,508	   +3.6	     189,617</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   214,477	  +17.9	     181,932</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		  463,496	  -32.9	     690,925</p>
<p>  Live cattle	     83,284	  +77.1		47,020</p>
<p>Since January 1994 CME has counted in volume anything that creates or liquidates open positions including expired options and SIMEX mutual offset transactions cleared on the CME.</p>
<p>Excluding these transactions, CME &quot;pit traded&quot; volume for February 1997 totaled 14,412,001.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago Derivatives Desk (312) 408-8750</p>
